      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\\) and express it in the form \\(a\\sqrt[4]{b}\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are positive integers. Let's go through the steps in detail.\n\nFirst, we write the expression inside the fourth root:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\n\\]\nWe know that the fourth root is equivalent to raising to the power of \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = (2^7 \\cdot 3^3)^{\\frac{1}{4}}\n\\]\nWe can use the property of exponents \\((a^m \\cdot b^n)^p = a^{mp} \\cdot b^{np}\\) to distribute the exponent \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\):\n\\[\n(2^7 \\cdot 3^3)^{\\frac{1}{4}} = 2^{7 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}} \\cdot 3^{3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}} = 2^{\\frac{7}{4}} \\cdot 3^{\\frac{3}{4}}\n\\]\nNext, we need to express \\(2^{\\frac{7}{4}}\\) and \\(3^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\) in a form that involves the fourth root. We know that:\n\\[\n2^{\\frac{7}{4}} = (2^7)^{\\frac{1}{4}} = (128)^{\\frac{1}{4}}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n3^{\\frac{3}{4}} = (3^3)^{\\frac{1}{4}} = (27)^{\\frac{1}{4}}\n\\]\nThus, we can write:\n\\[\n2^{\\frac{7}{4}} \\cdot 3^{\\frac{3}{4}} = 128^{\\frac{1}{4}} \\cdot 27^{\\frac{1}{4}} = \\sqrt[4]{128} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{27}\n\\]\nWe can express \\(128\\) and \\(27\\) as powers of smaller numbers:\n\\[\n128 = 2^7 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 27 = 3^3\n\\]\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{128} = \\sqrt[4]{2^7} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sqrt[4]{27} = \\sqrt[4]{3^3}\n\\]\nWe can rewrite these as:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7} = 2^{\\frac{7}{4}} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sqrt[4]{3^3} = 3^{\\frac{3}{4}}\n\\]\nCombining these, we get:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{128} \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{27} = 2^{\\frac{7}{4} + 0} \\cdot 3^{\\frac{3}{4} + 0} = 2^{\\frac{7}{4}} \\cdot 3^{\\frac{3}{4}}\n\\]\nSince \\(2^{\\frac{7}{4}} \\cdot 3^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\) can be written as:\n\\[\n\\frac{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}{2^4 \\cdot 3^4} = \\frac{128 \\cdot 27}{16 \\cdot 81} = \\frac{3456}{1296}\n\\]\nWe simplify the fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{3456}{1296} = \\frac{12}{5} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{6}\n\\]\nThus, \\(a = 5\\) and \\(b = 6\\), so:\n\\[\na + b = 5 + 6 = 11\n\\]\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]",
